<AssignMessage name="AM-ScanVerdict">
  <DisplayName>Record Model Armor scan state for logging</DisplayName>
  <!--
    MODEL ARMOR IS CURRENTLY REMOVED FROM THIS PROXY (2026-09-15). The scanning
    policies live in apigee/disabled/model-armor/ awaiting a Model Armor quota
    increase; see that directory's README and proxies/default.xml.

    This policy is retained on purpose even though there is nothing to read a
    verdict from. Every field below now resolves to its <Value> default,
    "disabled", because the referenced policies are not in the flow.

    WHY KEEP IT rather than drop the fields from ML-Attribution:

    1. "disabled" and "unset" mean different things, and the difference is the
       whole point. This log previously used "unset" to mean "the variable name
       is wrong for this Apigee version and needs confirming in a debug
       session" — i.e. a BUG. If the fields simply vanished, or silently read
       "unset", a future reader could not tell "we deliberately turned scanning
       off" from "the scan integration is broken". Those demand opposite
       responses.
    2. It keeps the llm-gateway-attribution log schema stable, so any query or
       dashboard built against scan_* keeps working across the removal and the
       eventual restore.
    3. It makes the unscanned period explicitly queryable after the fact:
       scan_prompt="disabled" marks every call that went through with no
       safety scanning, which is exactly the population anyone auditing this
       window will need to identify.

    ON RESTORE: revert this file to the verdict-reading version in
    apigee/disabled/model-armor/ (git history has it), which reads
    invocationResult and filterMatchState. Those two variable names were
    CONFIRMED from an Apigee debug session 2026-09-15, not inferred — the
    per-filter names tried first (raiFilterResult.executionState and friends)
    exist but are null in this Apigee version. Do not re-derive them.
  -->
  <AssignVariable>
    <Name>ma_prompt_result</Name>
    <Value>disabled</Value>
  </AssignVariable>
  <AssignVariable>
    <Name>ma_prompt_match</Name>
    <Value>disabled</Value>
  </AssignVariable>
  <AssignVariable>
    <Name>ma_response_result</Name>
    <Value>disabled</Value>
  </AssignVariable>
  <AssignVariable>
    <Name>ma_response_match</Name>
    <Value>disabled</Value>
  </AssignVariable>
  <AssignVariable>
    <Name>ma_prompt_failed</Name>
    <Value>disabled</Value>
  </AssignVariable>
  <AssignVariable>
    <Name>ma_response_failed</Name>
    <Value>disabled</Value>
  </AssignVariable>
  <IgnoreUnresolvedVariables>true</IgnoreUnresolvedVariables>
</AssignMessage>
